{"id":"film-series","title":"Highest-grossing film series","prompt":"Name the 10 film series and franchises that have grossed the most at the box office worldwide (all their films together)","noun":"film series","category":"Entertainment","metric":"Worldwide box office, all films","blitz":true,"source":{"name":"Wikipedia: List of highest-grossing films","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_highest-grossing_films","asOf":"2026-11-20"},"answers":[{"rank":1,"name":"Marvel Cinematic Universe","aliases":["Mcu","Marvel Comics cinematic universe","Marvel film universe","Marvel Extended Universe","Marvel Cinematic","Marvel Cinema Universe","Marvel Movie Universe","Marvel Cosmic Universe","Marvel Studios Cinematic Universe","Marvel","Marvel movies","Marvel films","The Infinity Saga","The Multiverse Saga"],"value":"$35,151,231,853","n":35151231853,"article":"Marvel Cinematic Universe","fact":{"text":"Marvel built it on the Avengers: it had licensed Spider-Man and the X-Men to Sony and Fox, but kept the Avengers.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marvel_Cinematic_Universe"}},{"rank":2,"name":"Spider-Man","aliases":["Spiderman","Spidey","Spidee","Spider-Man films","Spider-Verse","Spiderverse"],"value":"$13,673,574,191","n":13673574191,"article":"Spider-Man","fact":{"text":"Sony got Spider-Man's film rights from Marvel for $7 million in 1999.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spider-Man_in_film"}},{"rank":3,"name":"Star Wars","aliases":["StarWars","Star War","Star Wars series","Star wrs","Star Warian","Star Wras","Sar wars","Star Wars franchise","Star Wars chronology","Stars War","Stars Wars","Starswars","Disney Star Wars","Skywalker Saga","Star Wars films"],"value":"$10,748,764,874","n":10748764874,"article":"Star Wars","fact":{"text":"George Lucas started it in 1971, after he failed to get the rights to film Flash Gordon.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_Wars"}},{"rank":4,"name":"Wizarding World","aliases":["J. K. Rowling's Wizarding World","J.K. Rowling's Wizarding World","Harry Potter","Harry Potter films","Harry Potter series","Fantastic Beasts","Potter"],"value":"$9,661,430,799","n":9661430799,"article":"Wizarding World","fact":{"text":"Filming of Chamber of Secrets began just three days after the first Harry Potter film came out in 2001.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wizarding_World"}},{"rank":5,"name":"Avengers","aliases":["Avengers films"],"value":"$7,912,166,953","n":7912166953,"article":"Avengers (film series)","fact":{"text":"Endgame became the highest-grossing film ever in July 2019, until an Avatar re-release in China won it back in 2021.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avengers_(film_series)"}},{"rank":6,"name":"James Bond","aliases":["Bond. James Bond.","Mr bond","James bonf","Bond 007","Sir James Bond","James Bond 007","James Bond OO7","The name's Bond. James Bond.","Bond OO7","007 Bond","007 James Bond","OO7 James Bond","OO7 Bond","Bond","Bond films","James Bond films"],"value":"$7,836,510,562","n":7836510562,"article":"James Bond","fact":{"text":"Ian Fleming took the name from a bird book's author: he wanted the dullest name he could find.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Bond"}},{"rank":7,"name":"X-Men","aliases":["X-Men 4","X-men film series","X-Men trilogy","X-Men movies","X-Men films","Fox Men","X-men 5","X-Men Universe","X-Men Cinematic Universe","Xmen","Deadpool","Wolverine"],"value":"$7,422,190,386","n":7422190386,"article":"X-Men (film series)","fact":{"text":"Hugh Jackman wasn't the first Wolverine: Dougray Scott was cast until Mission: Impossible 2 ran late.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X-Men_(film_series)"}},{"rank":8,"name":"Fast & Furious","aliases":["Fast and the Furious","The Fast Saga","Fast & Furious 11","Fast 11"],"value":"$7,338,933,038","n":7338933038,"article":"Fast & Furious","fact":{"text":"The first film, in 2001, grew out of \"Racer X\", a 1998 Vibe magazine article about street racing.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fast_%26_Furious"}},{"rank":9,"name":"DC Extended Universe","aliases":["DC Cinematic Universe","DC Cinema Universe","DC Comics shared universe films","DC Comics' cinematic universe films","DC film universe","DC Cinematic Multiverse","DC Movie Universe","DCEU","DC Universe","DC movies","DC","DC Comics"],"value":"$7,197,660,384","n":7197660384,"article":"DC Extended Universe","fact":{"text":"When it was announced, fans and the media called it the DC Cinematic Universe, after Marvel's MCU.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DC_Extended_Universe"}},{"rank":10,"name":"Batman","aliases":["New Batman","Bruce wayne batman","Batman films","Dark Knight","The Dark Knight trilogy","Joker","DC","DC Comics"],"value":"$7,103,790,561","n":7103790561,"article":"Batman","fact":{"text":"He first reached cinemas in Columbia Pictures' Batman of 1943, followed by Batman and Robin in 1949.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batman_in_film"}}],"extras":[{"rank":11,"name":"Jurassic Park","aliases":["Jurassic World"],"value":"$6,878,119,429","n":6878119429},{"rank":12,"name":"Avatar","aliases":[],"value":"$6,744,195,218","n":6744195218},{"rank":13,"name":"Despicable Me","aliases":["Minions"],"value":"$6,156,215,672","n":6156215672},{"rank":14,"name":"Middle-earth","aliases":["Lord of the Rings","LOTR","The Hobbit"],"value":"$5,979,000,075","n":5979000075},{"rank":15,"name":"Transformers","aliases":[],"value":"$5,429,275,457","n":5429275457},{"rank":16,"name":"Mission: Impossible","aliases":[],"value":"$4,741,543,902","n":4741543902},{"rank":17,"name":"Pirates of the Caribbean","aliases":["POTC"],"value":"$4,522,015,850","n":4522015850},{"rank":18,"name":"Toy Story","aliases":[],"value":"$4,444,561,804","n":4444561804},{"rank":19,"name":"Shrek","aliases":["Puss in Boots"],"value":"$4,032,155,345","n":4032155345},{"rank":20,"name":"The Twilight Saga","aliases":["Twilight"],"value":"$3,365,550,566","n":3365550566},{"rank":0,"name":"The Lion King","aliases":[],"value":"$3,